{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"ba160afb-815f-40e9-8cb7-6b3e73590fa1","title":"Superposition of two waves: constructive and destructive"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ba160afb-815f-40e9-8cb7-6b3e73590fa1","step":{"id":"s1","script":"At one instant, compare two equal-amplitude waves. Superposition means adding their displacements at each position, not adding their heights wherever the peaks happen to be.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"inphase","region":"left","frame":{"x":[0,6.2832],"y":[-2.5,2.5],"axes":"edge","x_label":"phase x (rad)","y_label":"displacement / A"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_left","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.2832],"label":"wave 1"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.14,2.2],"text":"Constructive"}]},{"op":"figure","id":"opposite","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,6.2832],"y":[-2.5,2.5],"axes":"edge","x_label":"phase x (rad)","y_label":"displacement / A"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_right","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.2832],"label":"wave 1"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.14,2.2],"text":"Destructive"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"addition","anchor":{"el":"inphase","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"y_{\\mathrm{total}}(x)=y_1(x)+y_2(x)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ba160afb-815f-40e9-8cb7-6b3e73590fa1","step":{"id":"s2","script":"On the left, wave two exactly overlaps wave one. Peaks meet peaks and troughs meet troughs, doubling the amplitude: constructive interference.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"construct_marks","on":"inphase","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_two_left","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.2832],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"fn","id":"sum_left","y":"2*sin(x)","domain":[0,6.2832],"label":"sum"},{"kind":"point","id":"single_peak","at":{"on":"wave_left","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"point","id":"double_peak","at":{"on":"sum_left","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"single_peak"},"to":{"at":"double_peak"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[2.3,1.55],"text":"1 + 1 = 2","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"construct_eq","anchor":{"el":"addition","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"y_2=y_1=A\\sin x\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad y_{\\mathrm{total}}=2A\\sin x"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ba160afb-815f-40e9-8cb7-6b3e73590fa1","step":{"id":"s3","script":"On the right, wave two is half a cycle out of phase. Equal and opposite displacements cancel everywhere, producing complete destructive interference.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"destruct_marks","on":"opposite","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_two_right","y":"-sin(x)","domain":[0,6.2832],"stroke":"dashed","label":"wave 2"},{"kind":"fn","id":"sum_right","y":"0","domain":[0,6.2832],"label":"sum"},{"kind":"point","id":"positive_peak","at":{"on":"wave_right","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"point","id":"negative_peak","at":{"on":"wave_two_right","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"positive_peak"},"to":{"at":"negative_peak"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"sum_right","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"text","at":[3.14,-1.8],"text":"1 + (−1) = 0","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"destruct_eq","anchor":{"el":"opposite","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"y_2=-y_1\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad y_{\\mathrm{total}}=A\\sin x-A\\sin x=0"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What must be true for two waves to cancel completely?","expected_gist":"Equal amplitudes and opposite displacements everywhere."}}}
